# classic.list - a starting set of the old, well-known groups: one per line, the name and a
# description.  Used by create-groups.sh (makes them, read-only) and news-import --groups (keeps
# only articles posted to one of them).  Edit freely; what the archive you import does not have
# just stays empty.  "net.*" is the hierarchy before the Great Renaming of 1986-87.
#
# before the renaming
net.general         General discussion (the pre-1987 catch-all)
net.news            About Usenet itself
net.news.group      Discussion of creating and merging groups
net.jokes           Humor
net.unix            Unix
net.unix-wizards    Unix internals and bugs
net.lang.c          The C language
net.lang.lisp       Lisp
net.sources         Source code
net.micro           Microcomputers
net.micro.pc        The IBM PC
net.micro.mac       The Apple Macintosh
net.sf-lovers       Science fiction
net.music           Music
net.followup        Followups to older articles
net.wanted          Requests
net.misc            Miscellaneous
net.politics        Politics
net.religion        Religion
net.cooks           Cooking
net.games           Games
net.nlang           Natural languages
net.space           Space
